        "Content": "Glenmahon, John O' Connell Street, Cobh ,P24PT18 – Historic 4-Bed Residence with a Vast Rear Garden ,Unrivalled Cathedral & Panoramic Harbour Views, plus Premium Self-Contained Apartment Potential\r\n\r\nProperty Overview\r\n\r\nPamela Nel of Patrick Leonard Wilson Keenan Estate & Letting Agents is delighted to present Glenmahon, a highly distinguished and historic period residence steeped in Cobh's rich maritime heritage, boasting uninterrupted panoramic views across Cobh Harbour and the dramatic spires of St. Colman's Cathedral.\r\n\r\nOriginally known to the British Admiralty as \"Boatswain Lodge,\" this exceptional home occupies a prime position on the highly sought-after John O' Connell Street, immediately beside Cobh's historic Bible Garden. For generations of local residents, it was fondly known as the home of the beloved Mrs. McGann's Playschool.\r\n\r\nToday, this substantial four-bedroom residence effortlessly combines timeless character with remarkable versatility, offering a vast rear garden rarely seen in this area, together with a flexible annex layout ideally suited for multi-generational living, guest accommodation, or potential rental income.\r\n\r\n Ground Floor Accommodation\r\n\r\n Entrance Hallway – A bright and welcoming central hallway , creating an impressive sense of space while opening directly onto the expansive rear garden.\r\n\r\nElegant Lounge – A beautifully proportioned formal living room centred around a charming featured fireplace with lovely views out to the garden.\r\n\r\nFormal Dining Room – Featuring durable laminate flooring and a fully functioning fireplace, this inviting room serves as the heart of the home and provides access to the first-floor accommodation.\r\n\r\nKitchen & Glass Atrium – The solid wood fitted kitchen includes an eye-level oven and gas hob. Beyond lies a bright enclosed glass atrium, flooding the space with natural light while providing a peaceful transition into the beautiful garden.\r\n\r\nGround Floor Master Suite – An exceptionally spacious elevated double bedroom complemented by a private adjoining lounge, beautifully finished with rich wood panelling that adds warmth and character.\r\n\r\n First Floor Accommodation\r\n\r\n* Spacious double bedroom enjoying elevated views is fully carpeted and has built-in cupboards. \r\n\r\n* Two well-appointed single bedrooms, both fully carpeted and featuring ample storage cupboards.\r\n\r\n* The family bathroom is located on the ground floor.\r\n\r\n Annex / Apartment Potential\r\n\r\nPositioned discreetly beside the attached single garage is an exceptionally large utility room together with an adjacent bathroom. With direct access back into the main entrance hallway, this versatile wing offers excellent independent accessibility, making it ideal for conversion into a self-contained apartment, premium home office, or private granny flat (subject to any necessary permissions).\r\n\r\nExterior & Grounds\r\n\r\nVast Rear Garden – An exceptionally large elevated rear garden, rarely seen in this area, making it a true standout feature for a town-centre period home. The grounds enjoy spectacular uninterrupted views across Cobh Harbour and towards the iconic St. Colman's Cathedral.\r\n\r\nDirect Street Access – Positioned at the side of the garden, a secure private gate provides direct access to the street, offering exceptional convenience for gardening, deliveries, services, or an additional private entrance.\r\n\r\nLocation & Lifestyle\r\n\r\nJohn O'Connell Street enjoys one of the finest positions in one of Europe's most picturesque coastal towns, combining peaceful residential surroundings with immediate access to Cobh's vibrant town centre.\r\n\r\n* Excellent choice of preschools, primary schools and highly regarded secondary schools nearby.\r\n\r\n* A short stroll to local favourites including Seasalt Café & Deli, The Arch Café & Wine Bar, and the renowned Titanic Bar & Grill.\r\n\r\n* Cobh Train Station is within easy reach, providing regular commuter services to Fota, Little Island and Cork City Centre.\r\n\r\n* BER D energy efficiency \r\n\r\n Why Glenmahon?\r\n\r\nProperties of this historical significance, offering such exceptional views, generous accommodation, and a rear garden of this scale rarely seen in this area, seldom come to market. Glenmahon presents a unique opportunity to own a landmark home in one of Cork Harbour's most sought-after locations.\r\nEarly viewing is advised .\r\n\r\n***All information provided is to the best of our knowledge. The utmost of care and attention has been placed on providing factual and correct information. In certain cases some information may have been provided by the vendor to us. We do not hold any responsibility for mistakes, errors or inaccuracies in our online advertising and give each and every viewer the right to get an opinion on any concern they may have***"
      },
